Carafe Lab: bound every storage buffer binding to its mapped device range.
Explicit descriptors and the cbuf 0 size heuristic now share the layout and device-continuity
checks. The existing 8 MiB limit remains for unknown sizes; explicit NVN sizes can exceed it
when the mapping supports them. No size-only test can distinguish a valid NVN descriptor
from an NVK root-table word with the same bits. Zero sizes return the null binding before
alignment; the aligned prefix must also be contiguous, and binding sizes cannot wrap u32.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

